+/*
+ * ===================================================================
+ * RPI_IOC_DEBUG - compile-time switch for ALL Raspberry Pi hang
+ * diagnostics in this file (2026-04 .. 2026-10 hang hunt):
+ *   UART breadcrumb tracer, RAM crash ring at 0x28000000 that survives
+ *   a watchdog reset, GSNPSID write probe, overlap/NAK-holdoff fix
+ *   candidate, FIQ-FSM shadow state, per-channel diag counters and the
+ *   periodic "DWC_OTG t=" console dump, GAHBCFG core-mask helper.
+ * The hang itself was a bug in the RTEMS raspberrypi BSP interrupt
+ * dispatcher (bsps/arm/raspberrypi/irq/irq.c, fixed 2026-10-13), so
+ * none of this is needed for normal operation.  Define RPI_IOC_DEBUG
+ * here (and RPI_IOC_DEBUG=YES in the EPICS app Makefile, which also
+ * links irqwrap.c / fiq_gpio_toggle.c) to get the full instrumentation
+ * back.  What stays in production: the BCM2835 errata workarounds
+ * (AHB-idle wait, 4080-word FIFO cap, GAHBCFG 0x10) and the init
+ * summary line.
+ * ===================================================================
+ */
+/* #define RPI_IOC_DEBUG 1 */
+#ifdef RPI_IOC_DEBUG
